<https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-aspect/0.1.0/ont/core-owl> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0009-0003-7263-9946> .
<https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-aspect/0.1.0/ont/core-owl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Defines value aspects of lis:QualityDatum as OWL ontology\nBackground:\nThe Industrial Data Ontology (IDO) already establishes a clear distinction between properties (lis:Quality) and values (lis:QualityDatum).\nBuilding on this foundation, this ontology introduces aspects to further refine the semantics of values (lis:QualityDatum).\nAspects enable a more granular and standardized representation of value-related information,\nallowing for precise classification and contextualization of characteristics that describe specific values (lis:QualityDatum),\nsuch as ranges, thresholds, or other value-specific attributes.\n\nThis ontology aligns with IEC 61360-1, particularly its LEVEL_TYPE concept (MIN, NOM, TYP, MAX),\nwhich is now implemented more flexibly by representing each role as a separate class and\nsupporting all four values to enable precise semantic composition of value aspects.\n\nThis ontology is inspired by and extends the plm ontology from POSC Caesar Association (PCA)." .
<https://posccaesar.org/ontology/quality-datum-aspect/0.1.0/ont/core-owl> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/plm/ont/core> .
